\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two implementations of dense attention and three of top-$k$ attention, computing two functions in five ways. All five evaluate every pairwise score, because a score-then-select rule must form the complete score vector before it can rank it. They differ in what reaches memory and in how much arithmetic the aggregation performs, and only the gathered and fused top-$k$ variants execute the saving that motivates sparsification at all.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:taxonomy}{{1}{6}{Two implementations of dense attention and three of top-$k$ attention, computing two functions in five ways. All five evaluate every pairwise score, because a score-then-select rule must form the complete score vector before it can rank it. They differ in what reaches memory and in how much arithmetic the aggregation performs, and only the gathered and fused top-$k$ variants execute the saving that motivates sparsification at all}{figure.1}{}}
