\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Latency divided by the faster of the two dense implementations, against the number of peers retained. The dotted line is what an operation count predicts for the gathered path, $(N+k)/2N$, which lies below parity everywhere and so predicts a saving at every sparsity. Shading marks the region in which sparsity is actually faster; only the fused gathered kernel enters it, and only at the smallest $k$.}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
